### Triage service — manual examples (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Run the service (docker compose up -d postgres kafka redis, then the app) and execute the requests in order:
# the registration stores the new patient id in {{patientId}} for the following requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### RF-01 — Register example E1 (expected: 201, nivel CRITICO, slaMinutos 5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombreCompleto": "Ana Pérez",
  "edad": 45,
  "frecuenciaCardiaca": 130,
  "presionSistolica": 180,
  "presionDiastolica": 110,
  "spo2": 97,
  "temperatura": 36.8,
  "dolor": 8,
  "gcs": 15,
  "quejaPrincipal": "Dolor torácico"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("patientId", response.body.id);
%}

### RF-02 — Get the patient (expected: 200, estado REGISTRADO, tiempoEnEstadoActual like PT1M5S)
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}

### RF-02 — Start the consultation (expected: 200, estado EN_CONSULTA)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}/estado
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "estado": "EN_CONSULTA"
}

### RF-02 — Same status again (expected: 409, "No se puede pasar de EN_CONSULTA a EN_CONSULTA: ...")
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}/estado
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "estado": "EN_CONSULTA"
}

### RF-02 — Discharge (expected: 200, estado ALTA)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}/estado
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "estado": "ALTA"
}

### RF-02 — Invalid transition (expected: 409, "No se puede pasar de ALTA a EN_CONSULTA.")
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}/estado
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "estado": "EN_CONSULTA"
}

### RF-02 — Unknown status value (expected: 400, errors[0].campo = estado)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}/estado
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "estado": "CERRADO"
}

### RF-02 — Id that is not a UUID (expected: 400, errors[0].campo = id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/abc

### RF-02 — Unknown patient (expected: 404, "Paciente no encontrado")
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### RF-03 — Manual escalation test
# Start the service with a 1-minute CRITICO SLA and a short evaluation interval, e.g. from the repo root:
#   TRIAGE_SLA_CRITICAL=1 TRIAGE_ESCALATION_INTERVAL=PT5S ./mvnw -pl triage-service spring-boot:run
# (PowerShell: $env:TRIAGE_SLA_CRITICAL="1"; $env:TRIAGE_ESCALATION_INTERVAL="PT5S"; ./mvnw -pl triage-service spring-boot:run)
# 1. Register example E1 with the first request of this file (CRITICO, slaMinutos = 1) and keep its id in patientId.
# 2. Wait a bit more than 1 minute (+ up to one interval): the log shows "Escalated 1 overdue patient(s)".
# 3. Run the GET below: escalado = true, fechaEscalamiento set, estado still REGISTRADO.
#    The topic triaje.eventos gets one paciente_escalado with key = patientId; later cycles do not repeat it.
# 4. PATCH to EN_CONSULTA (RF-02 request above) still works and keeps escalado = true.
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/pacientes/{{patientId}}

### RF-05 — Operation report for one UTC day (expected: 200, 24 elements in horas, empty hours in 0 / null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/reportes/operacion?desde=2026-11-13T00:00:00Z&hasta=2026-11-14T00:00:00Z

### RF-05 — Same day grouped by Bogotá local hour (expected: 200, hora like 2026-11-13T00:00:00-05:00)
# A positive offset must be URL-encoded: +01:00 → %2B01:00
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/reportes/operacion?desde=2026-11-13T00:00:00-05:00&hasta=2026-11-14T00:00:00-05:00&zonaHoraria=America/Bogota

### RF-05 — Invalid parameters (expected: 400, errors for desde (missing), hasta (format) and zonaHoraria)
GET {{baseUrl}}/triage/reportes/operacion?hasta=2026-11-14&zonaHoraria=Mars/Base


